Worked on response times (ms): [22, 25, 28, 31, 33, 35, 38, 41, 45, 52, 61, 78, 120, 210, 400]. Sorted already. p50 (median) = **41** ms; p99 = **373.4** ms. The mean would be polluted by the 400 ms outlier; percentiles describe what users actually feel. SLO connection: a '99.9% of requests < 300 ms' objective is a percentile statement — an error budget of 0.1% means 0.015 bad requests allowed per 15 in this sample's scale. Measure percentiles on real data, never assume normality for latency.

