Worked example: A=[[1, 2], [3, 4]], B=[[5, 6], [7, 8]]. C[i][j] = Σ_k A[i][k]·B[k][j]. C[0][0] = 1×5+2×7 = **19**; C[0][1] = 1×6+2×8 = **22**; C[1][0] = 3×5+4×7 = **43**; C[1][1] = 3×6+4×8 = **50**. So AB = **[[19, 22], [43, 50]]**. Note BA differs: BA = [[23, 34], [31, 46]] — order matters. A matrix is a linear map; multiplication is composition of maps.

