Eigenvalues solve det(A − λI) = 0. For A=[[1, 2], [3, 4]]: (1−λ)(4−λ) − 6 = λ² − 5λ + (-2) ... precisely λ² − (trace)λ + det = 0, i.e. λ² − 5λ + -2 = 0. Discriminant 5² − 4×-2 = **33**. λ = (5 ± √33)/2 = **5.3723**, **-0.3723**. Check: λ₁+λ₂ = 5.0000 = trace ✓; λ₁×λ₂ = -2.0000 = det ✓. Eigenvalues are the scaling factors along the matrix's natural axes — the basis of PCA and stability analysis.

