Fit y = mx through points (1,2), (2,3), (3,5): minimize Σ(mxᵢ − yᵢ)². Normal equation: m = Σxᵢyᵢ/Σxᵢ². Σxᵢyᵢ = 1×2+2×3+3×5 = **23**; Σxᵢ² = 1+4+9 = **14**; m = 23/14 ≈ **1.6429**. Residuals: predictions 1.64, 3.29, 4.93 vs actual 2, 3, 5 — the best single slope in the least-squares sense. This is linear regression with one parameter; the full version solves (XᵀX)⁻¹Xᵀy. Data is vectors; models are matrix operations. This is the language.

