Your capstone has two workstreams. (1) **The modeling capstone:** given a set of query patterns for a marketplace (product catalog, orders, reviews, sellers), produce a full schema — which relationships embed, which reference, which indexes (ESR-ordered) — and defend each choice in writing. (2) **The application capstone:** build a working PyMongo app against that schema with bulk ingestion, an aggregation analytics endpoint, and transactions only where correctness demands them. Deliverable: the schema document, the repo, and a short write-up of what the explain plans taught you.

